    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="In the creeping-flow limit Re = 2R|v|/\nu \ll 1, the nonlinear advection term in the Navier-Stokes equations is negligible next to viscous diffusion, leaving the linear Stokes equations \mu\nabla^2\mathbf{u}=\nabla p -- George Stokes&#x27; 1851 exact solution for uniform flow past a sphere of radius R, giving a drag force">

