.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Concentrating a 2D flow&#x27;s vorticity into point vortices turns the vorticity-transport PDE into an N-body system: each vortex simply advects with the velocity induced by every other vortex through the 2D Biot-Savart law,">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/fluids/vortex_dynamics/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_von_karman_street_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/fluids/vortex_dynamics/plot_von_karman_street`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">A von Karman vortex street holds its shape</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/fluids/vortex_dynamics/plot_von_karman_street`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="An isolated point vortex of circulation \Gamma induces a purely azimuthal velocity of magnitude \Gamma/(2\pi r) at distance r (the 2D Biot-Savart law); for two vortices separated by distance d, this is exactly the speed each one advects with, carried by the field of the other. What the pair then does depends only on the relative sign of their circulation. Equal circulations \Gamma each orbit the common midpoint at radius d/2, so their induced speed \Gamma/(2\pi d) translates into a rigid-body angular velocity">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/fluids/vortex_dynamics/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_vortex_pair_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/fluids/vortex_dynamics/plot_vortex_pair`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Co-rotating pair versus translating dipole</div>
    </div>


